---
import CaseStudyLayout from "../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro";
---

<CaseStudyLayout
	title="Vanguard 3.1: Self-Service Business Intelligence • Case Study"
	breadcrumbs={["Apple InfoSec", "Vanguard 3.1", "Lead Product Designer"]}
>
<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<!-- SECTION 1: HERO & TITLE                               -->
			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<article class="case-section">
				<!-- Kicker & Tag -->
				<div
					class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 mb-4"
				>
					<span class="m-0">Project Vanguard</span>
				</div>

				<!-- Main Title -->
				<h1>Making Security Work Measurable</h1>

				<!-- Lead Paragraph -->
				<div class="case-prose max-w-4xl mb-10">
					<p>
						The InfoSec organization at Apple struggled to answer
						one question: <em>"How are we keeping Apple safe?"</em>.
					</p>
					<p>
						I led design for a <strong
							>self-service analytics platform</strong
						> that answered it though coverage and on-time commentary
						on metrics. The platform simplified metric management and
						paired AI-generated insights with human validation. Security
						leaders used it to plan efforts, investments, and priorities
						with confidence.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Hero Visual -->
				<figure class="m-0 mb-4">
					<div class="media-frame">
						<img
							src="/images-vanguard/vg1_homepage.png"
							alt="Vanguard Homepage Interface - Executive Security Health Overview"
							loading="eager"
						/>
					</div>
					<figcaption>
						Vanguard: Central executive dashboard displaying
						governed security metrics with live trust tiers and
						anomaly alerts.
					</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<!-- Metadata Matrix Box: Role and Timeline Panel -->
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mt-16">
					<div>
						<span class="kicker">role</span>
						<strong class="font-bold text-black text-sm block mb-1"
							>Lead Product Designer</strong
						>
						<span class="text-black/75 block leading-relaxed"
							>Strategy, interaction model, governance design.</span
						>
						<span class="text-black/50 block mt-1"
							><time>2025 Q3</time> - <time>2026 Q2</time></span
						>
					</div>
					<div>
						<span class="kicker">team</span>
						<strong class="font-bold text-black text-sm block mb-1"
							>Core &amp; Partner Teams</strong
						>
						<span class="text-black/75 block leading-relaxed"
							>1 Designer (me), 4 Developers, 2 Data engineers, 1
							PM, 1 SME, partner security orgs.</span
						>
					</div>
					<div>
						<span class="kicker">outcome</span>
						<div
							class="text-emerald-700 font-bold text-sm block mb-1"
						>
							BI Coverage: 30% → 75%
						</div>
						<span class="text-black/75 block leading-relaxed"
							>Escalation calls during incidents cut by more than
							half. Onboarding dropped from 2 months → 5 days.</span
						>
					</div>
				</div>
			</article>

			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<!-- SECTION 2: CONTEXT                                    -->
			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<article class="case-section">
				<div class="case-grid">
					<!-- Left 25% Column -->
					<div class="case-sidebar">
						<span class="kicker">context</span>
						<h2>Vanguard Business Intelligence (BI)</h2>
					</div>

					<!-- Right 75% Column -->
					<div class="case-content">
						<div class="case-prose">
							<p>
								The BI team's charter was to publish performance
								metrics for senior leadership and partner teams
								to help make strategic, forward-looking
								decisions.
							</p>
							<p>
								They closely worked with each partner team to
								hand-build metrics - defining the measure,
								negotiating the formula, working with multiple
								data engineering teams, publishing, and handling
								ongoing maintenance.
							</p>
							<p>
								<strong
									>Metrics published in Vanguard were the
									single source of trusted truth for Apple
									leadership.</strong
								>
							</p>
						</div>

						<!-- Images: Side by Side -->
						<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5 pt-2">
							<figure class="m-0">
								<div class="media-frame">
									<img
										src="/images-vanguard/vg2_mttd_metric.png"
										alt="Mean Time to Detect (MTTD) Metric View"
									/>
								</div>
								<figcaption>
									Single Metric Detail View (MTTD)
								</figcaption>
							</figure>

							<figure class="m-0">
								<div class="media-frame">
									<img
										src="/images-vanguard/vg2_programs.png"
										alt="Vanguard Security Programs Inventory"
									/>
								</div>
								<figcaption>
									Vanguard Security Programs Catalog
								</figcaption>
							</figure>
						</div>
						<figcaption class="text-left mt-2">
							Early Vanguard metrics and program structures were
							manually maintained by a central BI squad.
						</figcaption>
					</div>
				</div>
			</article>

			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<!-- SECTION 3: THE PROBLEM                                -->
			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<article class="case-section">
				<div class="case-grid">
					<!-- Left 25% Column -->
					<div class="case-sidebar">
						<span class="kicker">problem</span>
						<h2>
							Executives had no defensible way to answer ‘How are
							we keeping Apple safe?’
						</h2>
					</div>

					<!-- Right 75% Column -->
					<div class="case-content">
						<div class="case-prose">
							<p>
								The small BI team could only cover <strong
									>~30% of the security teams</strong
								>. Others ended up creating their own dashboards
								to share with leadership directly. Executives
								were struggling for one holistic view they could
								trust.
							</p>
						</div>

						<!-- Design Goals Aside -->
						<aside>
							<span
								class="font-departure text-xs font-bold tracking-wider text-black block mb-3"
							>
								My Design Goals:
							</span>
							<ul
								class="space-y-3 font-sans text-base text-black/85 list-none pl-0 m-0"
							>
								<li class="flex items-start gap-3">
									<span
										class="font-departure text-black font-bold"
										>01.</span
									>
									<span
										><strong>Increase BI coverage</strong> - through
										simplified or faster onboarding.</span
									>
								</li>
								<li class="flex items-start gap-3">
									<span
										class="font-departure text-black font-bold"
										>02.</span
									>
									<span
										><strong
											>Design and implement a holistic
											view for leadership</strong
										> - using a top-down results map.</span
									>
								</li>
								<li class="flex items-start gap-3">
									<span
										class="font-departure text-black font-bold"
										>03.</span
									>
									<span
										><strong
											>Improve the platform interface</strong
										> - to better the dashboards of non-BI teams.</span
									>
								</li>
							</ul>
						</aside>

						<!-- Images: Results Map & Incident Management -->
						<div
							class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-12 gap-5 pt-2"
						>
							<div class="sm:col-span-7">
								<figure
									class="m-0 h-full flex flex-col justify-between"
								>
									<div class="media-frame">
										<img
											src="/images-vanguard/vg3_results_map.png"
											alt="Top-down Results Map for Leadership"
										/>
									</div>
									<figcaption>
										Holistic leadership view: mapping
										strategic goals to measures
									</figcaption>
								</figure>
							</div>

							<div class="sm:col-span-5 flex flex-col gap-5">
								<figure class="m-0 flex-1">
									<div class="media-frame">
										<img
											src="/images-vanguard/vg3_impact_metrics.png"
											alt="Impact Metrics Breakdown"
										/>
									</div>
									<figcaption>
										High-level security impact metrics
									</figcaption>
								</figure>

								<figure class="m-0 flex-1">
									<div class="media-frame">
										<img
											src="/images-vanguard/vg3_incident_management.png"
											alt="Incident Management Dashboard"
										/>
									</div>
									<figcaption>
										Non-BI team dashboard integration
									</figcaption>
								</figure>
							</div>
						</div>
						<figcaption class="text-left mt-2">
							Connecting top-level strategic security objectives
							to team-level operational metrics.
						</figcaption>
					</div>
				</div>
			</article>

			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<!-- SECTION 4: RESEARCH                                   -->
			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<article class="case-section">
				<div class="case-grid">
					<!-- Left 25% Column -->
					<div class="case-sidebar">
						<span class="kicker">research</span>
						<h2>Metrics went stale, and anomalies unexplained</h2>
					</div>

					<!-- Right 75% Column -->
					<div class="case-content">
						<div class="case-prose">
							<p>
								I started with a <strong>design sprint</strong> with
								the BI team to align on goals and map how a metric
								actually gets made. Then I ran interviews on both
								ends of the pipe.
							</p>
							<p>
								I found onboarding was slow (<strong
									>average 2 months</strong
								>) primarily due to iteration between the two
								teams. Also, different teams had a variety of
								dashboards - using varied metrics across the
								board.
							</p>
							<p>
								My conversations with partner teams and
								executives uncovered two underlying challenges:
							</p>
						</div>

						<!-- Two Core Challenges Cards -->
						<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
							<aside class="m-0">
								<h3
									class="font-departure text-sm font-bold text-black m-0 mb-2"
								>
									1. Published metrics went stale soon
								</h3>
								<p
									class="font-sans text-sm text-black/75 leading-relaxed m-0"
								>
									Teams had to spend a lot of time
									continuously working with the BI team to
									maintain their metrics, and back-and-forth
									caused more friction than help.
								</p>
							</aside>

							<aside class="m-0">
								<h3
									class="font-departure text-sm font-bold text-black m-0 mb-2"
								>
									2. Anomalies were displayed, but not
									explained
								</h3>
								<p
									class="font-sans text-sm text-black/75 leading-relaxed m-0"
								>
									When a metric spiked, there was a flurry of
									questions, check-ins, and chaos as
									leadership wanted to understand the full
									picture.
								</p>
							</aside>
						</div>

						<!-- Images: Research Discovery & Latency -->
						<div class="space-y-5 pt-2">
							<figure class="m-0">
								<div class="media-frame">
									<img
										src="/images-vanguard/vg5.png"
										alt="Research Findings: Onboarding Friction and Maintenance Choke Points"
									/>
								</div>
								<figcaption>
									Mapping the metric authoring lifecycle and
									identifying failure points
								</figcaption>
							</figure>

							<figure class="m-0">
								<div class="media-frame">
									<img
										src="/images-vanguard/vg6.png"
										alt="Metric Workflow and Back-and-Forth Handoff Friction"
									/>
								</div>
								<figcaption>
									The 2-month handoff bottleneck between
									partner teams and central BI
								</figcaption>
							</figure>
						</div>
						<figcaption class="text-left mt-2">
							Visualizing the iterative bottlenecks that made
							central metrics lag operational realities.
						</figcaption>
					</div>
				</div>
			</article>

			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<!-- SECTION 5: STRATEGY & REFRAMING                       -->
			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<article class="case-section">
				<div class="case-grid">
					<!-- Left 25% Column -->
					<div class="case-sidebar">
						<span class="kicker">strategy</span>
						<h2>The team had two plans. I argued for one.</h2>
					</div>

					<!-- Right 75% Column -->
					<div class="case-content">
						<!-- Design Sprint Dialogue Box -->
						<div class="card">
							<div
								class="font-departure text-xs tracking-wider text-black/50 pb-3 mb-4 border-b border-black/15 font-semibold"
							>
								Main points from the Design Sprint Debate
							</div>
							<div class="space-y-4 text-base">
								<div class="p-3 border-l-2">
									<strong
										class="font-departure text-xs block text-black/60 mb-1"
										>Director</strong
									>
									<p class="m-0 text-black/90">
										"More BI headcount cannot solve the
										bottleneck problem, since teams are
										looking for autonomy and control."
									</p>
								</div>
								<div class="p-3 border-l-2">
									<strong
										class="font-departure text-xs block text-emerald-800 mb-1"
										>Me, Director, Dev Lead</strong
									>
									<p class="m-0 text-black/90 font-medium">
										"Let's expand to a self-service
										platform!"
									</p>
								</div>
								<div class="p-3 border-l-2">
									<strong
										class="font-departure text-xs block text-amber-800 mb-1"
										>Product Manager</strong
									>
									<p class="m-0 text-black/90">
										"That will dilute the trust factor we
										gained over years."
									</p>
								</div>
							</div>

							<div class="mt-6 pt-5 border-t border-black/15">
								<span
									class="font-departure text-xs tracking-wider text-red-700 font-bold block mb-1"
								>
									The Fundamental Question:
								</span>
								<p
									class="italic text-lg italic text-black/90 m-0"
								>
									"If anyone can publish, why would an
									executive believe anything?"
								</p>
							</div>
						</div>

						<div class="c">
							<p>
								We also collectively agreed to bring in <strong
									>AI-powered anomaly detection and analysis</strong
								>.
							</p>
							<div
								class="border-l-2 border-dashed border-black/40 pl-5 py-3 bg-white border border-black/10 p-4"
							>
								<span
									class="font-departure text-xs tracking-wider text-black/60 block mb-1 font-semibold"
								>
									Reframed Design Challenge:
								</span>
								<p
									class="text-xl sm:text-2xl text-black font-semibold m-0"
								>
									"How might we make governance and trust
									signals visible in a scalable business
									intelligence platform?"
								</p>
							</div>
						</div>

						<!-- Images: Strategic Architecture & Trust Signals -->
						<div class="space-y-5 pt-2">
							<figure class="m-0">
								<div class="media-frame">
									<img
										src="/images-vanguard/vg61.png"
										alt="Strategic Architecture: Governance and Trust Model"
									/>
								</div>
								<figcaption>
									Architectural framework for self-service
									with embedded governance
								</figcaption>
							</figure>

							<figure class="m-0">
								<div class="media-frame">
									<img
										src="/images-vanguard/vg62.png"
										alt="Governing Trust Signals in a Scalable BI Platform"
									/>
								</div>
								<figcaption>
									Detailed interaction model mapping trust
									tiers directly into user workflows
								</figcaption>
							</figure>
						</div>
						<figcaption class="text-left mt-2">
							Strategy: Moving from gatekeeper reviews to visible,
							embedded provenance signals.
						</figcaption>
					</div>
				</div>
			</article>

			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<!-- SECTION 6: DESIGN 1/4 - QUALITY GATES                 -->
			<!-- ===================================================== -->
			<article class="case-section">
				<div class="case-grid">
					<!-- Left 25% Column -->
					<div class="case-sidebar">
						<span class="kicker">design</span>
						<h2>1. Quality gates built into the onboarding flow</h2>
					</div>

					<!-- Right 75% Column -->
					<div class="case-content">
						<div class="case-prose">
							<p>
								Rather than reviewing quality after submission,
								I baked checks directly into the authoring path.
								The self-serve flow asks the same questions the
								BI team used to ask in review meetings:
							</p>
						</div>

						<!-- 3 Checks Cards -->
						<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
							<aside class="m-0 p-4">
								<span
									class="font-departure text-xs text-black/50 block mb-1"
									>CHECK 01</span
								>
								<strong
									class="font-sans text-sm text-black block"
									>Formula Clarity</strong
								>
								<p
									class="font-sans text-xs text-black/70 mt-1 m-0"
								>
									Is there an explicit, unambiguous formula
									for this measure?
								</p>
							</aside>
							<aside class="m-0 p-4">
								<span
									class="font-departure text-xs text-black/50 block mb-1"
									>CHECK 02</span
								>
								<strong
									class="font-sans text-sm text-black block"
									>Data Provenance</strong
								>
								<p
									class="font-sans text-xs text-black/70 mt-1 m-0"
								>
									Are all contributing data sources declared?
								</p>
							</aside>
							<aside class="m-0 p-4">
								<span
									class="font-departure text-xs text-black/50 block mb-1"
									>CHECK 03</span
								>
								<strong
									class="font-sans text-sm text-black block"
									>Baseline Calibration</strong
								>
								<p
									class="font-sans text-xs text-black/70 mt-1 m-0"
								>
									What does "good" look like, and against what
									baseline?
								</p>
							</aside>
						</div>

						<!-- Six Onboarding Steps: Side-by-Side Grid -->
						<div
							class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-2"
						>
							<figure class="m-0 flex flex-col justify-between">
								<div>
									<div
										class="flex items-center justify-between pb-2 mb-2 border-b border-black/15 font-departure text-[10px]"
									>
										<span class="font-bold text-black"
											>01. Measure</span
										>
										<span class="text-black/50"
											>Formulas</span
										>
									</div>
									<div class="media-frame mb-2">
										<img
											src="/images-vanguard/vg_contribute_1.png"
											alt="Step 1: Formula definition and verification"
										/>
									</div>
								</div>
								<p
									class="font-sans text-xs text-black/75 m-0 leading-normal"
								>
									Partner teams define measures with clear
									formulas and data sources.
								</p>
							</figure>

							<figure class="m-0 flex flex-col justify-between">
								<div>
									<div
										class="flex items-center justify-between pb-2 mb-2 border-b border-black/15 font-departure text-[10px]"
									>
										<span class="font-bold text-black"
											>02. Thresholds</span
										>
										<span class="text-black/50"
											>Baselining</span
										>
									</div>
									<div class="media-frame mb-2">
										<img
											src="/images-vanguard/vg_contribute_2.png"
											alt="Step 2: Baseline targets and anomaly limits"
										/>
									</div>
								</div>
								<p
									class="font-sans text-xs text-black/75 m-0 leading-normal"
								>
									Baseline calibration sets statistical
									control limits and alert bands.
								</p>
							</figure>

							<figure class="m-0 flex flex-col justify-between">
								<div>
									<div
										class="flex items-center justify-between pb-2 mb-2 border-b border-black/15 font-departure text-[10px]"
									>
										<span class="font-bold text-black"
											>03. Ownership</span
										>
										<span class="text-black/50"
											>DRI Assignment</span
										>
									</div>
									<div class="media-frame mb-2">
										<img
											src="/images-vanguard/vg_contribute_3.png"
											alt="Step 3: Direct Responsible Individual (DRI) assignment"
										/>
									</div>
								</div>
								<p
									class="font-sans text-xs text-black/75 m-0 leading-normal"
								>
									Every metric requires a named DRI
									responsible for investigations.
								</p>
							</figure>

							<figure class="m-0 flex flex-col justify-between">
								<div>
									<div
										class="flex items-center justify-between pb-2 mb-2 border-b border-black/15 font-departure text-[10px]"
									>
										<span class="font-bold text-black"
											>04. Automation</span
										>
										<span class="text-black/50"
											>Pipelines</span
										>
									</div>
									<div class="media-frame mb-2">
										<img
											src="/images-vanguard/vg_contribute_4.png"
											alt="Step 4: Continuous data pipeline validation"
										/>
									</div>
								</div>
								<p
									class="font-sans text-xs text-black/75 m-0 leading-normal"
								>
									Continuous queries poll endpoints to ensure
									zero data drift.
								</p>
							</figure>

							<figure class="m-0 flex flex-col justify-between">
								<div>
									<div
										class="flex items-center justify-between pb-2 mb-2 border-b border-black/15 font-departure text-[10px]"
									>
										<span class="font-bold text-black"
											>05. Audit Trail</span
										>
										<span class="text-black/50"
											>Lineage</span
										>
									</div>
									<div class="media-frame mb-2">
										<img
											src="/images-vanguard/vg_contribute_5.png"
											alt="Step 5: Change history and version logging"
										/>
									</div>
								</div>
								<p
									class="font-sans text-xs text-black/75 m-0 leading-normal"
								>
									Formula revisions and pipeline edits are
									immutably versioned.
								</p>
							</figure>

							<figure class="m-0 flex flex-col justify-between">
								<div>
									<div
										class="flex items-center justify-between pb-2 mb-2 border-b border-black/15 font-departure text-[10px]"
									>
										<span class="font-bold text-black"
											>06. Certification</span
										>
										<span class="text-black/50"
											>Publication</span
										>
									</div>
									<div class="media-frame mb-2">
